{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1340778-a-gradual-start","id":1340778,"title":"A Gradual Start","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-11T08:10:56-07:00","id":1340778,"title":"A Gradual Start","content":"When and if I do try and introduce my group to Exalted, I'm thinking it might be best to start slow and sort of ease them into the system, rather than bludgeoning them over the head with 15 charms at once. What do you guys think of a schedule like...<br /> <br /> <b>Sessions 1~4:</b> <b>Pure Mortals</b>, to get used to the basic system. Make sure people are comfortable with the withering/decisive distinction, use of intimacies, and so on, so that when the time comes to choose Charms they can have some idea of what they're dealing with. Stat-wise, I'm thinking 6/6/4 dots for Attributes, 28 dots for Abilities, four Specialties, and... 6 dots for merits, maybe?<br /> <br /> <b>Session 5: Basic Exalts</b>. No charms besides Excellencies and Anima Powers, to get everyone used to flow of essence and the *real* scale of the system. Stat-wise, you get your Caste and your skills, another 2 dots for your primary Attribute, the rest of your Merit dots, and the full set of Bonus Points.<br /> <br /> <b>Session 6: Supernals</b>. Everyone picks their Supernal ability and 5 Charms from that Ability.<br /> <br /> <b>Session 7: Charms</b>. Everyone picks their remaining 10 &quot;starting&quot; Charms.<br /> <br /> <b>Session 8~12: Growth</b>. Double XP progression. Give everyone a chance to finish fleshing things out a little faster than normal, to make up for the slow start.<br /> <br /> <b>Session 13+</b>: <b>Normal</b>. Standard XP progression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T08:54:13-07:00","id":1340788,"title":"","content":"That seems okay, there are a LOT of systems in Exalted though, so you might want to stretch the mortal time depending on how many people are doing wildly different things. If one is a crafter/loremaster, another is a sailor/socialite, and another is a doctor/strongman you\u2019ll have a lot of explaining to do. Also if they\u2019re new to tabletops in general and not just exalted specifically you might want it to go really really slow and maybe not even introduce things like onslaught penalties and stuff at first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T08:57:52-07:00","id":1340789,"title":"","content":"I would recommend spacing out the acquisition of starting Charms more than your current plan of giving 5 and 10 Charms over 2 sessions.<br /> <br /> What worked well in my group is having everyone gain 3 Charms when Exalting, then getting 1 free Charm per game alongside normal exp for the next 12 sessions. That way players never have to learn more than 1-2 new Charms per game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T11:01:19-07:00","id":1340804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1340778-a-gradual-start?p=1340788#post1340788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems okay, there are a LOT of systems in Exalted though, so you might want to stretch the mortal time depending on how many people are doing wildly different things. If one is a crafter/loremaster, another is a sailor/socialite, and another is a doctor/strongman you\u2019ll have a lot of explaining to do. Also if they\u2019re new to tabletops in general and not just exalted specifically you might want it to go really really slow and maybe not even introduce things like onslaught penalties and stuff at first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh gods, I would <i>not </i>want to try and teach first-time-roleplayers Exalted right off the bat <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I've been running a 5e game with some newbies for almost a year now and the Monk and Barbarian <i>still </i>don't really understand all their abilities.<br /> <br /> As for subsystems... the only two that I think would be really tricky are War, Sail, and &lt;shudder&gt; Crafting. But either way, at least for those I can take the player aside and work though it with them one-on-one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1340778-a-gradual-start?p=1340789#post1340789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would recommend spacing out the acquisition of starting Charms more than your current plan of giving 5 and 10 Charms over 2 sessions.<br /> <br /> What worked well in my group is having everyone gain 3 Charms when Exalting, then getting 1 free Charm per game alongside normal exp for the next 12 sessions. That way players never have to learn more than 1-2 new Charms per game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. That's not a bad idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T14:28:00-07:00","id":1340843,"title":"","content":"What interests you about Exalted?<br /> <br /> Because playing mortals is a very different experience to playing the Chosen.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd just run the intro game with the pregened characters as a sampler of what Exalted is all about, then see if people want to make their own characters and have a proper game.<br /> <br /> Nothing wrong with your way, but four sessions of Mortal: The Bleedening, then two sessions of Baby's First Superpowers might be a brillant way of showcasing the game's mechanics but it's not hitting my idea of what Exalted is all about. You're going to have to work hard to keep the game interesting whilst continually adjusting player expectations about what their characters can do.<br /> <br /> Played right, your idea is amazing.<br /> But it's a lot more work than just playing the published adventure specifically designed to teach people the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-12-2019, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T14:46:39-07:00","id":1340845,"title":"","content":"I greatly enjoy the way combat flows, the sheer richness of noncombat abilities represented by Charms, the availability of fully-fleshed-out mechanics for things like ships and mass combat... *I* enjoy all that, and I think my players will too, but... I have two main concerns.<br /> <br /> First is character creation. There are a frankly terrifying number of Charms, and a lot of them are on the arcane side even after you understand the rest of the system. I want my players to be able to make informed choices, to actually have some idea about how the wheels work before they go shopping for superchargers.<br /> <br /> My second is speed. Ex3 (especially in combat) can be slow at the best of times. I'd like to get it moving at a decent clip before we start complicating things with piles and piles of situational Charms to keep track of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T18:39:24-07:00","id":1340883,"title":"","content":"Charm choice isn't <i>so</i> bad. Especially if you use mad letters cascades. Though choosing their starting charms in bunches over the first few sessions shouldn't break too much. Maybe gate supernal stuff for a couple of sessions?<br /> <br /> Are they gonna be solars? Because dragon bloods start play at essence 2 to keep a level playing field. (Also there are mortal creation and conversion guidelines on page 125 of core)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24967-general-trivia-kit","name":"General Trivia Kit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T23:54:15-07:00","id":1340915,"title":"","content":"A lot of people do something like this, it generally works well.<br /> Myself, with my current game I gave them 10 charms to start with and 1 free charm per session for 5 session. That seemed to work.<br /> <br /> I will say though, that while being mortals to start with works in terms of teaching tone, I think that mortals are actually a bit more complex than Exalts with no charms (bleeding, infection).<br /> <br /> It might be easier to start as exalts with no charms, then in the second game introduce excellencies, then give them 1-3 charms a session (and possibly no xp) until they have 15.<br /> <br /> If you are worried about the sheer number of charms, getting them to just choose a small number at a time might help. You're probably going to have to help them choose, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T05:03:20-07:00","id":1340930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1340778-a-gradual-start?p=1340915#post1340915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will say though, that while being mortals to start with works in terms of teaching tone, I think that mortals are actually a bit more complex than Exalts with no charms (bleeding, infection).<br /> <br /> It might be easier to start as exalts with no charms, then in the second game introduce excellencies, then give them 1-3 charms a session (and possibly no xp) until they have 15.</div> </div> </div> </div>This causes me much less concern. Seems much easier to run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T06:28:29-07:00","id":1340938,"title":"","content":"I'll also say that how difficult they'll find charms probably depends on concept.<br /> <br /> In my current game, I've got one player who's always got cool ideas, stunts, etc, but struggles to remember what all his charms do in combat. Luckily, he's playing a tough, strong Full Moon, who has a lot of permanent charms, so it's not too bad. The Lunar charms that swap a stat, Ox-Bodies, things like the Dodge charm that causes people to lose initiative when they miss you, these tend to be easier to remember.<br /> <br /> I'll also say that out-of-combat stuff is generally easier to use, because you're not trying to juggle 5 things in your head, and also characters who are more all-round (some combat charms, some social, some other stuff) are easier to handle because in each situation you're just thinking of 3-4 possible things, rather than 15.<br /> <br /> I also find that my players struggle with a)dice caps when combining different charms, especially anything with successes, and b)grappling.<br /> I definitely do not advise new or non-mechanically-inclined players to build a grappler. Also I guess Stealth is a bit complex, but it's easier for players than grappling.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}